  "scaleNote": "This is a 250 m Terra MODIS NDVI point sample at an approximate Mount Apo summit-area reference coordinate, not a mapped burn perimeter or a confirmed burned pixel. NDVI measures vegetation greenness; it does not detect active fire, quantify burned area, or establish fire damage or ecological recovery. The reported March 2016 fire affected a broader area, and the sources do not establish whether this point was inside it. Steep terrain, cloud cover, mixed land cover, and thin monthly composite support can further limit interpretation. Only good- or marginal-reliability 16-day observations contribute to monthly means; marginal observations are less certain, and months without accepted observations remain gaps.",
